{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021831-metis-produced-through-war-crimes-and-unchanged-kin","id":1021831,"title":"Metis Produced Through War Crimes and Unchanged Kin","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-24T22:02:43-08:00","id":1021831,"title":"Metis Produced Through War Crimes and Unchanged Kin","content":"Two thorny issues concerning the conception of Metis<br /> <br /> A) Though not often mentioned, it has been acknowledged that just as in wars between Humans, Post-Battle Rape *is* also a sad reality of Garou Warfare. So it would be irresponsible to dance around the issue that yes, more than a few Metis would probably have been children cocieved in violence.<br /> But herein lies the dilemma:<br /> <br /> As it is written/chiseled/clawed, &quot;Garou Shalt Not Mate With Garou&quot; brings shame upon BOTH parties for <i>willingly</i> breaking Taboo <i>Numero-Uno</i> set down by Gaia herself, and both parents are henceforth stigmatized as &quot;Charach&quot;, only slightly higher on the social totem pole than the &quot;bastards&quot; they conceived.<br /> <br /> The assaulter is irrefutably a Charach ON-TOP of being a filthy rapist worse than an animal, but what of the Assaulted Mother (and very occasionally, Father) of the Metis Child?<br /> <br /> 1) Would the Rape Victim also be branded a &quot;Charach&quot; by the Garou Nation, as they DID technically Mate with A Garou, however unwillingly?<br /> <br /> 2) Would he/she bear the mark of shame of being a &quot;Charach&quot; if the child is carried to term?<br /> <br /> 3) Heck, what about the poor Metis Child in question if the father/mother decides to love/raise him/her in spite of never intending his/her birth in the first place? Would they be treated with any kindness or (Gaia Forbid) *worse* than a Metis conceived through a loving-union?<br /> <br /> B) You *never* know if a Kinfolk is Garou until their first change, and yet it is stated that unchanged Garou who mate with another Garou (changed or not) STILL produce Metis despite the fact they are not yet Shapeshifters.<br /> And no doubt, *completely* un-intended accidents can and DO happen thanks to arranged marriages of daughters/sons &quot;who never got the gift&quot;, and the tragic results not revealed until that fateful day nine-months-later in the delivery room.<br /> <br /> So:<br /> <br /> 1) Since the father/mother in question is not even a Garou at the time, and does not even KNOW he or she is a Garou on that fateful night, does he or she *still* get punished as a &quot;Charach&quot; in spite of being technically guiltless in the birth of a Metis?<br /> <br /> 2) How much shame is there in circumstances like these wherein *neither* parent is technically guilty of *willingly* breaking the litany?<br /> <br /> 3) Severe emotional shock/trauma/pain is a common trigger for The First Change; so at the risk of sounding crass, does the often horrific and traumatic pain of chidbirth count as one of the tirggers of the First-Change? (For teenage moms, for example) At the very least it would certainly help an unknowing-Garou Mom survive the birth of her &quot;surprise monster baby.&quot;<br /> <br /> C) Finally, in Tribes like the Get of Fenris it is said that taking responsibility and raising your Metis Child is a responsibility that BOTH parents have to shoulder. Since what is done is done, and both are more than likely to NEVER be allowed to honorably marry any kin again, are there formally performed Marriage Ceremonies between Garou who stay together for their Metis *outside* the Children of Gaia (who of course respect True Love), so at the very *least* their love for each other is recognized and ratified?<br /> <br /> Phew too much sugar from Christmas Pudding gets the brain racing.<br /> <br /> Merry Christmas Everybody! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 12-25-2016, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T00:34:52-08:00","id":1021887,"title":"","content":"It breaks down to two parts forming your answer. There is the formal outcome, and the informal outcome.<br /> <br /> Formally, it is done. All involved are branded Charach since they broke the litany. Willingness isn't exactly a question. They are both warriors of Gaia, so there are no excuses. By the way, among the Garou there is no reason to think that one gender suffer this more than the other.<br /> <br /> Informally, it will vary wildly depending on community and circumstances. Some will place all the blame on one parent and completely forgive the other. After all, ignoring the litany is as much of a tradition as following it. This can be done out of hate, compassion or prejudice, even political plays.<br /> <br /> Unknowing parents due to unexpected Change are more likely to be pardoned. But the marriage will never be deemed valid. One failure isn't reason to not try right next time.<br /> <br /> A Metis pregnancy forces the mother to Crinos in the very last weeks, so this mother WILL Change either way, now. And the Metis is still what it is, there is no reason for a change in status. The child of parents who knew what they were doing isn't more guilty. Guilt isn't a factor for the Metis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T02:40:46-08:00","id":1021908,"title":"","content":"From what I've seen and read, rape is not treated the same as a willing Litany breach. First of all, rape is Wyrmy and therefore the rapist has let the Wyrm control them in that act. The act of making a metis out of love is not an act of corruption, no matter what some Fianna say. But an act of rape is, so the blame would solely go to the rapist. And given that this is a strategy Black Spiral Dancers use at times, it happens.<br /> <br /> The victim is another matter entirely, depending on whether they are female or male. For males, it will possibly not even be mentioned or they are even given renown if they stood the act with dignity. If the mother isn't a Dancer, they are possibly killed on the spot. Any child born will be judged VERY harshly and aren't the responsibility of their father. Maybe even killed, just to be safe to avoid more Wyrmtaint. Of course the male will deal with PTSD, but generally they are expected to get over it eventually.<br /> <br /> For female victims, it is a harder pill to swallow. They aren't to blame, but given they are carrying a child made by a Wyrmish act, they are left with hard choices. Some in more traditional tribes might perform the Rite of Winter Wolf to preserve their honor, or go on a suicide mission. They might try to perform an abortion by claws and silver. Or they can try to raise the child.<br /> <br /> The child will have to live with the stigma of their origin, and be judged as potential betrayers in traditional tribes.<br /> <br /> As for pre-changers, they are going to be blamed still. Mainly because they SHOULD have known the other was a pre-changer, if they had been good kinfolk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T07:36:54-08:00","id":1021979,"title":"","content":"I do not think that rape would be possible again a post-change Garou. In the one cases where it has come up in my games, I had them automatically enter into a frenzy and shift into Crinos. I gave the Garou two points of Rage every turn that their potential attackers were alive, even if it temporarily pushed them above their maximum Rage, and they did not leave frenzy until everyone who was guilty of the crime.<br /> <br /> It was a game in the late-90s set in the Kosovo War. A group of characters, one of the Black Furies, we're sent to rescue a village of Kinfolk before the Serbs could commit genocide against them. The characters were captured by a company of Serbian soldiers and the sole female (the Black Fury) was taken away. Skip ahead, she goes into frenzy and slaughters the entire company.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T09:03:48-08:00","id":1022003,"title":"","content":"I'm going to say a character's first sexual experience is emotional enough to trigger first change. <br /> <br /> This solves the &quot;I didn't know I was Garou!&quot; issue, but causes all sorts of &quot;teenagers, don't have sex issues or bad things may happen&quot;. And everyone knows how difficult it is to keep teenagers from having sex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T09:50:50-08:00","id":1022017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021831-metis-produced-through-war-crimes-and-unchanged-kin?p=1021979#post1021979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think that rape would be possible again a post-change Garou. In the one cases where it has come up in my games, I had them automatically enter into a frenzy and shift into Crinos. I gave the Garou two points of Rage every turn that their potential attackers were alive, even if it temporarily pushed them above their maximum Rage, and they did not leave frenzy until everyone who was guilty of the crime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I brought up the issue because Garou on Garou assaults was addressed in the &quot;Garou Shalt Not Mate With Garou&quot; entry of &quot;Tribebook Get Of Fenris First Edition&quot;, wherein it is said that a Black Fury <i>successfully</i> sued and found guilty a Get of Fenris who raped her; the Fenrir granted her justice by allowing her to &quot;take his weapon away from him.&quot;<br /> <br /> I was quite taken back that *First* Edition Get of Frenris would find rape to be repulsive, considering the Vikings from whom they descended COINED the Stereotype of &quot;Killing Pillaging and Raping Barbarians in Longboats&quot; into the Western Modern Subconcious, and *First* Edition Get of Fenris were basically Vikings with serial-numbers filed off multiplied by Nazism.<br /> <br /> Naturally it's impossible/pointless/stupid (and top of being already repulsive and despicable) for a human to even try: even against the weakest Crinos (Strength 5, Human Maximum) it would be like Pee Wee Herman trying to rape Arnold Schwarzenegger. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 12-25-2016, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T10:53:07-08:00","id":1022037,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a>, considering that the theme is Garou with Garou, nothing makes it impossible for raping Crinos being also in Crinos. It would be exceedingly violent, but such are the Garou. Your houserule, though, works well to keep this from the game without seeming silly.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4684\" data-vbnamecard=\"4684\">Lin Liren</a>, the Vikings didn't coined such stereotype at all. Actually, all kinds of violence are commonplace in war zones, soldiers do a lot of despicable things, and it have being this way since wars happened for the first time. Rape is, actually, a very sad &quot;classic&quot; of war. Both against defenseless civilians and captured enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T11:10:14-08:00","id":1022042,"title":"","content":"I think that a Garou in frenzy would be too dangerous for another Garou to attempt to rape, even if they are both in Crinos. Even if there are large differences in strength and soak, Garou against Garou fights are deadly. At worst, the potential rapist kills their victim and violates the corpse. At best, the victim kills the potential rapist and everyone around them. Of course, you can run things differently, but I can think of few things that would cause Garou to lose control more than the threat of rape against themselves or their loved ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T12:12:38-08:00","id":1022052,"title":"","content":"I think incidents of Garou on Garou rape would be much more rare than rape in the real world. Rape happens because the attacker is more physically powerful than the victim. Sexual dimorphism means women are generally less strong than men. In war zones, the men have guns and are in units so multiple men can assist each other. Female Garou do not have such a relative disadvantage. (I know male on male rape also happens in prisons and other places, but again is generally targeted against weaker men and often in combination with numbers).<br /> <br /> Garou for the most part are all trained in combat. There is going to be far more female Garou who know how to fight, some very well. They are all going to capable of dealing aggravated damage if they are in Crinos - so even far more powerful Garou know they have the risk of getting some very serious injuries. So there is a much higher likelihood of death for the assailant. And of course there is the issue of auspice and gifts. I find it hard to believe that a male Ragabash, no matter how physically bigger, defeating a female Ahroun. And of course there is frenzy whic is not something that can be controlled and will eithe result in the death of the perpetrator or victim. Criminals look for easy victims, not people who look like they can fight back.<br /> <br /> Another issue is that there are unlikely to be any&quot;civilian&quot; Garou just standing about after combat. If another pack or sept is invading, then all the Garou of the pack or sept will be fighting back. If they are defeated, the female Garou is likely either to be dead or in flight with the survivors, not remaining in the area. It is always possible a Garou will be captured, but I don't think that is very likely.<br /> <br /> Lastly, the Garou operate under a system of privately enforced justice. There is no official police force and judiciary which can at times, unfortunately, frustrate justice because of limitations of what they can or can't do. If you rape another Garou, that Garou's pack or sept (or possible even local tribemates) is going to come after you. That won't dissuade everyone from such acts, but it is going to be a factor for many.<br /> <br /> Since sexual relations between Garou is a huge taboo, I don't see the sept elders back home tolerating this either when the victorious Garou come back home.<br /> <br /> I think abducting and raping female kinfolk to be much more likely. They are much more defenseless. They are less likely to lead to feuds as the other side's family would be more likely to accept some kind of deal. And they don't run the risk of violating that part of the Litany.<br /> <br /> If rape happens, it is likely to be the result not of physical acts, but assertion of dominance by Pure Breed, intimidation, staredown, etc. that makes the female Garou &quot;naturally&quot; submit to something she wouldn't otherwise. Of course, whether that counts as rape in Garou culture is itself problematic (here different tribes would act differently, I don't think Black Furies would tolerate that while a Shadow Lord would). In such cases, Garou would likely treat it as an ordinary case of Litany violation, not a crime against the victim.<br /> <br /> If it does happen regardless of the method, I think the reputation of the victim will probably depend on the tribe or sept. While some victims may be ostracized because they should have fought it off or escaped, I very doubt that the Children of Gaia or Black Furies would find the victim guilty. Even the Get of Fenris, who are seen to be especially devoted to their own people, I believe would side with the victim. On the other hand, tribes particularly obsessed with notions of honor or dislike of Metis, like the Fianna, Silver Fangs, or Shadow Lords, might shame the victim.<br /> <br /> As for Metis children resulting from it, if there is such a thing as Garou abortion, I think it is going to be practiced here. I don't think a female Garou is going to carry any baby she doesn't want to carry. And having an abortion might be essential in demonstrating the person was not at fault. Very, very, very few such metis are going to be carried to term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T13:15:20-08:00","id":1022069,"title":"","content":"Well, I think that surgical abortion would be required for pregnant female Garou, as their systems would probably prevent chemical abortions from being effective. Unlike female humans, female Garou probably could have benefited from surgical abortion as early as the Paleolithic Era, as flint flakes are razor sharp, and as they would been much less likely to die from complications such as excessive bleeding and internal infections, so every Tribe would have quietly used abortion when the pregnancy would have resulted in Metis. Which does make it strange that any Metis would actually be born, since it is so shameful for Garou to bear Metis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T13:27:55-08:00","id":1022072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021831-metis-produced-through-war-crimes-and-unchanged-kin?p=1022042#post1022042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that a Garou in frenzy would be too dangerous for another Garou to attempt to rape, even if they are both in Crinos. Even if there are large differences in strength and soak, Garou against Garou fights are deadly. At worst, the potential rapist kills their victim and violates the corpse. At best, the victim kills the potential rapist and everyone around them. Of course, you can run things differently, but I can think of few things that would cause Garou to lose control more than the threat of rape against themselves or their loved ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Item 1: A Silver Fang-turned BSD attempts to rape Zhyzhak in the 2nd edition Book of the Wyrm intro fiction. If not for Zhyzhak having superhuman might in human form, it was conceivable that he could have gone through with it instead of being torn to pieces.<br /> <br /> Item 2: Rape isn't always by force. Using Doppleganger to look like someone's lover or spouse in the manner of some of Zeus's acts would constitute rape by fraud, for example, and there are both social Gifts and no shortage of circumstances, such as status and connections to higher-status members of society, that could be bent toward coercion.<br /> <br /> The bottom line is that no one is invulnerable or immune to all hazards of the world. That the list of candidates that can perpetrate such acts is generally smaller rules nothing out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T13:30:59-08:00","id":1022075,"title":"","content":"First, I want to make it clear that I'm not saying that it is common. Certainly it doesn't go even near of as common as among humans. I'm saying it does make sense to happen.<br /> <br /> By the OP itself, we are also talking about it in a very specific context: Garou vs Garou warfare. So we are not talking about rape as it happens commonly. We are talking it in the context of a war and, considering that we are talking Garou vs Garou, we're talking about rape against other warriors.<br /> <br /> Even among humans, most of those things apply. Most soldiers would go to extremes to avoid such a fate. It isn't abhorrent just for women, it is for men, too. And both can be present at war, in Garou society even more so. Even then, rape happens.<br /> <br /> Winners gang up on captured losers. They mount up on pressure. They beat to unconsciousness and then proceed. There are several ways a person can be violated, sexually or not. As Black Fox said, there are other ways than physical violence. Rage and Crinos can make things escalate, but they are not unavoidable. And they play at both sides. The aggressor can also use Gifts, Rage, and everything else. Frenzy is more of a lost of control than an asset. Yes, the victim will want the agressor dead, but for this to happen, the aggressor already achieved to be at an advantage.<br /> <br /> It isn't about the victim not fighting. Rape, on such situations, happens when the fight is already over.<br /> <br /> And for the litany, it depends on a lot of things. Probably most aggressors expect to have a way to avoid issues, mainly through no one ever knowing it happened. Most victims never tell no one it happened, and prideful people is even worse at this. So if a Garou do this to other after a battle with only pack and ally as witnesses, if no one talks about the incident back at sept, there is no justice to be done. Even if the victim talks when found, they are not from the same sept, and it won't be easy to proof what happened. It is more likely that the victim will want revenge personally, and it won't be easy to get. Even if done, it doesn't change what happened. Lies, excuses, pressure, killing witnesses, there will always be a lot of ways to get out with impunity. And there is the fact that sometimes the rape itself happens for rage and vengeance and such, and maybe the aggressor doesn't even care about the eventual consequences anymore. All of this result in the thing happening, even if the aggressor actually fails at getting scot-free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T13:43:37-08:00","id":1022081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021831-metis-produced-through-war-crimes-and-unchanged-kin?p=1022069#post1022069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think that surgical abortion would be required for pregnant female Garou, as their systems would probably prevent chemical abortions from being effective. Unlike female humans, female Garou probably could have benefited from surgical abortion as early as the Paleolithic Era, as flint flakes are razor sharp, and as they would been much less likely to die from complications such as excessive bleeding and internal infections, so every Tribe would have quietly used abortion when the pregnancy would have resulted in Metis. Which does make it strange that any Metis would actually be born, since it is so shameful for Garou to bear Metis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably it didn't happened for simpler reasons:<br /> <br /> 1- No way to know it was a Metis until it was almost there. Garou aren't very monogamist today, they were even less in the past. Breaking the Litany doesn't mean your only sexual partner was the other Garou. Probably most Metis had a pretty good chance of being actually common offspring (Homid, Lupus or Kinfolk).<br /> <br /> 2- Do such would only harm the community even more. The surgery needed to get rid of a pregnancy when the mother have such an astounding capacity for regeneration wouldn't be simple nor guaranteed. And it would take time of the mother far from the sept, would weak her, and probably also took time from eventual helpers.<br /> <br /> In the end, vanishing before the time when the mother would be constantly at Crinos would be suspicious enough by itself, and the mother would weight far more on the sept than carrying it to the end. Far easier to get rid of the child at birth and let the mother fight at suicidal missions as soon as she locks in Crinos, to cleanse her shame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T14:12:41-08:00","id":1022087,"title":"","content":"I think that the female would suspect that the pregnancy was caused by the rape if she was raped before she found out about the pregnancy, so she would probably rather bear the risk of aborting a 'normal' baby rather than suffer the shame of bearing a Metis child. The mother would only have regenerative capabilities in Crinos form, so Paleolithic cultures could probably do the surgery, though it would probably be lethal to anyone who was not Garou. While it would be odd for a Garou to leave her pack for a week without telling anyone, I am sure that it occurs frequently enough that it would not cause that much comment.<br /> <br /> I am not quite sure that the Garou would be that much against abortion under normal circumstances, at least for female Garou (abortions for female Kinfolk, or female Humans who were impregnated by male Garou, may be another subject in some Tribes). Statistically speaking, it is much more likely that Garou will be born from Garou males mating with human females rather than the mating of Garou females with human males. Historically, Garou females could bear one child in the same time than Garou males could sire eight children if we assumed one mating per day, though the existence of birth control would change that calculation in modern times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T21:19:49-08:00","id":1022207,"title":"","content":"Just chiming in to agree that Garou on Garou rape is going to happen a lot less than rape in our world. For a lot of the reasons already mentioned (by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> especially).<br /> <br /> The fact that is against the Litany is particularly important since that means such rapes are against the proposed aggressors own laws (in addition to the victim's). Spirals are obviously exempt, and most probably account for nearly all such cases. But for the rest of the (Gaian) Garou, it isn't just a matter of victims keeping silent. The rapist's own pack would be expected to step in and stop them (this is part of a Philodox's job). There is no reasoning that is going to excuse such a deliberate and flagrant violation of the Litany. The losers in a Garou war/battle aren't going to be the ones to suffer. The Kinfolk almost certainly will. But that's outside of the focus of this thread.<br /> <br /> Now a few points, without backtracking and quoting all over the place.<br /> If a Garou was raped and found out she were pregnant, I don't think the shame of bearing Metis would be put on her. Not exactly. Assuming she weren't in a hard line Tribe/Sept (where she might be required to kill the child at birth), she would be expected to raise said kid to be a productive member of society. I don't see Garou going the abortion route.<br /> <br /> On the not knowing who is Garou pre-change and who isn't. It hasn't been that way in a few editions. It would take 2 lost cubs hooking up pre-change (a fairly low probability) to have a chance of that scenario happening. I think that situation is rare enough that it would make for an interesting story for players to come across. It certainly isn't going to come up terribly often.<br /> <br /> I think child birth has a decent chance to trigger a first change, but it isn't guaranteed. First Changes in general are uncertain things, so there is no reliable way to trigger them, even wiith knowing someone is Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T00:08:16-08:00","id":1022239,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a>, first it would be a very particular decision. There is no such a thing as a paleolithic woman with the active sexual life of a warrior suspecting that a pregnancy came from the rape. Too much variables here can throw of any calculation, specially at such a time, and this woman would now this. Yes, she can <u>vaguely</u> suspect, but the chance of a good and healthy baby is still too good. Some would still try to get rid of the child, but it is to go too far to imagine that most would.<br /> <br /> You're also hugely underestimating such a surgery. It isn't something she can easily do alone, to begin with. And precisely because she won't regenerate in breed form (she can be a Lupus, to make things more complicated), she can die horribly from such a surgery. Oh, and getting rid of her regeneration won't account for the regeneration of the child, since a Metis regenerates &quot;since always&quot;.<br /> <br /> Finally, it isn't a question of statistics to look down on abortion for the Garou. Her child is the child of a Garou. Even if a male can repeat such a feat more frequently, it's still the child of a Garou. And what is more for their society at such an early age, it is a child whose mother is sturdy enough to increase significantly the chances of success on the birth. The mother wouldn't be barred from abortion, though. Parenting is saw as something completely optional among werewolves. But a child is a great social boon for the parents, so it would raise a good amount of questions all things considered.<br /> <br /> The hard-line here is that killing the newborn child is far easier and safer than abortion at the time, specially for a Garou. And a completely acceptable thing at old societies. A baby could be so killed simply for being an unhealthy Kinfolk. A Metis would be killed by most Garou on-spot, while the parents &quot;only&quot; get a (very severe) reprimand and social stigma. And while the baby isn't born the mother can as easily as get rid of it through surgery as through an accident during a mission. It is already established that Metis' mothers throw themselves into suicidal missions with abandon.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar805_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"805\" data-vbnamecard=\"805\">idpersona</a>, my arguing about the Litany is based on situations where it can be ignored by the involved. The situations we're discussing are already exceptional by definition, and in those situations a lot of psychological phenomenon can play a role to make what is, not surprisingly, dubbed sometimes as &quot;pack mentality&quot;. It isn't unbelievable that an entire pack is prone to deny the Litany if even a single member of the pack is so inclined, be it because of social dynamics, authority effects or pack culture. And the Garou break the Litany. That's all. It is a serious law, and it's breaking is a serious matter, but it happens anyway. Not common, though.<br /> <br /> Now, I don't think that it would be common at all for the victim to be blamed, much less severely so. But it is a situation already very complex IRL, imagine among the Garou societies. I can imagine some Garou blaming the outsider of their tribe/sept/pack by default, or some Furies blaming the man equally by default. And reactions can also vary because it happening is one thing, it being disclosed for full knowledge of all members is another. Most, though, if aware of all that transpired, would probably be extremely light with the victim, and maybe even ignore the part of the Litany on the punishment. <i>Strictly</i> going by the Litany, though, there is no such lenience. It is why a law system needs an interpretative judicial body, but the interpretation is up to their understanding of intent. Some can be light, but still brand the victim as Chalach because so says the law.<br /> <br /> Pre-changing mothers would probably Change for a Metis conception for a very simple reason. The mother of a Metis Changes to Crinos quite some weeks before giving birth because the baby is a Crinos itself. If the mother doesn't Change by then, she will likely die, and not have another chance to Change, never. It still can make for an interesting drama, though. A Kinfolk mother suddenly start to feel horribly wrong and dies like a month before giving birth, and the people caring for her suddenly have in their hands a premature Crinos baby, maybe pointing to the sudden discovery that someday the father will Change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T09:09:37-08:00","id":1022365,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>, I agree with almost everything you've said, so I will skip past the bulk of it (though it is important to reiterate that conquering Garou raping the losing side Garou would be exceedingly rare/nonexistent outside of Spirals).<br /> <br /> Some commentary on the last paragraph:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021831-metis-produced-through-war-crimes-and-unchanged-kin?p=1022239#post1022239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Pre-changing mothers would probably Change for a Metis conception for a very simple reason. The mother of a Metis Changes to Crinos quite some weeks before giving birth because the baby is a Crinos itself. If the mother doesn't Change by then, she will likely die, and not have another chance to Change, never. It still can make for an interesting drama, though. A Kinfolk mother suddenly start to feel horribly wrong and dies like a month before giving birth, and the people caring for her suddenly have in their hands a premature Crinos baby, maybe pointing to the sudden discovery that someday the father will Change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because changing would save a Garou's life doesn't mean that their First Change is ensured. So there is still a chance the Garou will die when the Crinos child grows too large for the homid womb (and I'm not sure of the viability of said child surviving). Again, I certainly think this will <i>could</i> (and probably would) bring on the First Change. It's just isn't 100%.<br /> On the very last line, the local Garou should already know the father will change. Scent of True Form (from Revised on) will know the child is Garou from birth. Revised took away a lot of the mystery of determining which &quot;kinfolk&quot; who would be Garou or not. Which is why I said this scenario would have to take place between 2 lost cubs meeting and having sex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 12-26-2016, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T09:56:50-08:00","id":1022378,"title":"","content":"In the end I mostly explored dramatic options. I agree that the Change of the mother is likely, but not guaranteed, and I agree that the survival of the child isn't guaranteed either. As I said, it is a premature baby. The baby can need medical attention as any premature child, though it is valid to remember that today IRL there are situations where the mother dies weeks before giving birth and the baby is successfully removed from the corpse and put into premature care, so the baby certainly can live not only because it is a Metis Garou, but because of swift medical attention.<br /> <br /> My point is the dramatic result. The surviving mother have to deal with the discovery of her condition. A father who didn't knew, the same. The couple surviving, the validity of their marriage becomes an issue. The baby surviving will have this story upon it, one way or the other. But if the surviving party doesn't discover nothing new about itself, the effect is watered down a little. It becomes just a quirk in someone's background. Can have some lasting effects, sure, like any traumatic past, but not much more to explore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}